/**
 * Reference EXR files written by the OpenEXR 3.x library (Python bindings),
 * base64-encoded. Used to verify the decoder against real encoder output.
 *
 * rgb_*   10x37 HALF R/G/B: R = x/10, G = y/37, B = 0.25 + ((x + y) % 3) * 0.25
 * yc_*    10x38 luminance/chroma: Y = 0.2 + x/20 + y/100 (full res);
 *         RY = 0.1 + sx*0.05 + sy*0.002, BY = -0.05 + sy*0.01 - sx*0.003,
 *         2x2 subsampled (sx = x >> 1, sy = y >> 1)
 * tiled_* 45x37 HALF R/G/B (same formulas as rgb_*), 16x16 tiles
 * mp_*    two-part file, both DECREASING_Y; part 0 = rgb_* formulas
 * noise_* 24x40 R = HALF noise, G = FLOAT noise (same content in every file)
 *
 * Suffix _inc/_dec = INCREASING_Y / DECREASING_Y line order.
 */

